{
  "documents": [
    {
      "title": "Agreed website scope",
      "text": "Project: website for Luntian Lantern Studio\nSeller: Mira Velan, independent web designer in the Philippines\nBuyer: Nilo Saren, owner of Luntian Lantern Studio\nAgreed fee: USD 640\n\nRequirements:\n- Deliver a homepage with an introduction, service summary, and contact details.\n- Deliver a working contact form that sends inquiries to payer-1@example.test.\n- Deliver a website that passes a keyboard-only accessibility review.\n- Deliver a gallery with six finished project photos and captions.\n\nThe fee covers the build and handover of the site files. The buyer will supply the business copy and project photos. Any work beyond these requirements will be quoted separately."
    },
    {
      "title": "Website handover note",
      "text": "Handover from Mira Velan to Nilo Saren\nProject: Luntian Lantern Studio website\n\nThe site files and a short setup guide are in the shared handover folder. The folder contains the homepage, gallery page, stylesheets, and image assets supplied for the project.\n\nHomepage delivered: introduction, service summary, and contact details are included.\nContact form: not delivered; the site has no contact form.\nAccessibility: the handover folder includes an accessibility report attachment, but the report text is not reproduced in this note.\nGallery: four of the six project photos have captions; the other two gallery slots are empty.\n\nThe setup guide explains how to publish the files. Please review the pages and tell me if anything in the supplied copy needs correction."
    },
    {
      "title": "Post-delivery chat",
      "text": "Nilo, 10:14: Thanks, I can open the handover folder and the homepage files.\nMira, 10:19: Good. The setup guide is in the same folder if you want to publish the site.\nNilo, 10:26: I see the four gallery photos. I will resend the remaining two images this afternoon.\nMira, 10:31: Thanks. I can add them after we agree on the next steps.\nNilo, 10:38: I also noticed there is no contact form. Please let me know when you can discuss that.\nMira, 10:44: I am available tomorrow morning. We can go through the outstanding items and the publishing instructions together."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
